      "title": "RTC false colour (display)",
      "description": "A rendering, not a measurement. Eight-bit display codes under a fixed stretch, WEBP-compressed, with an alpha band marking absent data. Channels are in decibels, unlike every other raster in this catalog: R = RTC VV over -18.5 to -5 dB, G = RTC VH over -26 to -11 dB, B = VV-VH dB. Backscatter spans about two and a half decades of linear power, so a linear eight-bit stretch would collapse nearly all glacier ice into the darkest few codes. The conversion is applied here and only here; the float32 assets stay linear.",
